{
 "source": "mail.png",
 "notes": [
  "Pieces every Court view shares. chrome/court_back is the way back out of a Court view: the mail painting's quiet plate (dark navy, steel rim, gold chevron) with its painted word lifted, so the word is set in type by CourtBack (client/scripts/ui/court_back.gd, layout client/layout/court_back.json) -- BACK until the COURT tab exists, then COURT, in one place.",
  "The word COURT was painted at x 222..304, caps y 109..127 (18 tall), ivory #F2F0EA; it is erased row by row from the plate's own navy on each side of it (x 206..214 and 311..318, ramped between them), which keeps the plate's vertical gradient; the chevron (x 184..202) stays painted.",
  "The store painting's own back plate (gold-rimmed, 166x59 at 174,105) is not cut: one plate for every Court view, where the mail has always drawn it (165,106).",
  "The COURT tab (client/scenes/tabs/court.gd, layout court.json) is cut from court.png: the header scene with ROYAL COURT and its line baked (the three pills Telea-filled under the shell's own), six cards each cut round its frame's outer rim (the chamfer 12 units, as painted), and the foot's foliage. The painting drifts: the left column's frames span x 171..531, the right's 545..911; rows start at 487, 843, 1199 and run 343, 345, 351 tall; each card is drawn where it was painted.",
  "Each card's red count disc is lifted (court/badge is card 2's, cut clean, and drawn with the count only when something waits): the frame under it is the same card's top-left corner mirrored about the card's own axis (x' = 702 - x on the left, 1457 - x on the right -- measured, the rims of both sides match to the pixel there), laid as three pieces -- the top rims, the right rims and the corner scroll -- and what is left of the disc (a crescent of picture) is Telea-filled from its surroundings and softened, which reads as the picture's own out-of-focus corner."
 ],
